00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:18,500
Chaos loves company.

2
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Borderlands is a action, science fiction, comedy film directed by Eli Roth.

3
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:43,500
Returning to her home planet, an infamous bounty hunter forms an
unexpected alliance with a team of unlikely heroes.

4
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Together, they battle monsters and dangerous bandits to protect a
young girl who holds the key to unimaginable power.

5
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:08,500
Lilith, played by Cate Blanchett.

6
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Roland, played by Kevin Hart.

7
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:33,500
Atlas, played by Edgar Ramírez.

8
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Tannis, played by Jamie Lee Curtis.

9
00:37:52,500 --> 00:37:58,500
Tiny Tina, played by Ariana Greenblatt.

10
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:11,000
Krieg, played by Florian Munteanu.

11
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:23,500
Borderlands is a 2024 American science fiction comedy film directed and
co-written by Eli Roth, based on the video game series.

12
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Cate Blanchett stars as Lillith, an outlaw who forms an alliance with a team of misfits
to find the missing daughter of the most powerful man in the universe.

13
00:54:42,500 --> 00:54:48,500
The ensemble cast also features Kevin Hart, Jack Black, Edgar Ramirez, Ariana
Greenblatt, Florian Munteanu, Gina Gershon, and Jamie Lee Curtis.

14
00:58:55,000 --> 00:59:01,000
The film was announced in August 2015, with Leigh Whannell in talks to direct.

15
01:03:07,500 --> 01:03:13,500
By February 2020, Roth was attached to direct from a screenplay by Craig Mazin.

16
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Casting took place from May 2020 to April 2021, with
Blanchett cast first and others the following year.

17
01:11:32,500 --> 01:11:38,500
Principal photography began in April 2021 in Budapest, Hungary,
during the COVID-19 pandemic, and wrapped in June.

18
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
Two weeks of reshoots took place in early 2023, directed by Tim
Miller due to Roth's commitments to Thanksgiving.

19
01:19:57,500 --> 01:20:03,500
That June, Mazin removed his name from the project
and was replaced by Joe Crombie.

20
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:16,000
Borderlands premiered at the TCL Chinese Theatre in Los Angeles, California on August 6,
2024, and was released in the United States by Lionsgate on August 9.

21
01:28:22,500 --> 01:28:28,500
The film received negative reviews from critics and grossed $33
million against a budget of $110–120 million.

22
01:32:35,000 --> 01:32:41,000
The film explores themes of outlaw, based on video game,
unlikely friendship, talking robot, malicious.

23
01:36:47,500 --> 01:36:53,500
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
